<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46977" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμερ-ινός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of day</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					508c
				</span></i>
			; <i>by day</i>, opp. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυκτερινός, πυρετός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Epid.</u>
					1.5
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγγελος ἡ</span>.
			<i>day</i>-messenger, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.6.18
			</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμεροδρόμος; ἡ. θεωρίαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					9.14.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοηλάται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PLond.</u>
					3.1177.153
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ. σῖτα</span>, in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				163
			</span></i> (anap.), is expl. by Sch., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θνητά,
				ἐπίγεια</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμερίων</span>
			)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; ἰχθύς ἡ</span>. is dub. in <i><span class="en">
				Ephipp.
				5.2
			</span></i> (anap.).</div>
